     1	"""Power analysis for paper §3 — minimum detectable effect (MDE) at α=0.05, β=0.20.
     2	
     3	For binary success rate comparisons (P-SoM vs best-baseline), computes:
     4	- MDE in percentage points at observed N per site
     5	- Per-cell power for assumed effect sizes (1pp / 2pp / 3pp / 5pp)
     6	- Family-wise power for K-of-N pass rule (H1: K_h1=12 of 16 cells, H3: K_h3=11 of 16)
     7	
     8	Method: paired-design McNemar-equivalent normal approximation (within-cell tasks
     9	are paired across modes since same task gets all modes). Power computed via
    10	exact binomial for K-of-N family rule.
    11	
    12	Usage:
    13	    python3 scripts/analysis/power_analysis.py
    14	    python3 scripts/analysis/power_analysis.py --baseline-sr 0.30 --output paper_section3_power.md
    15	
    16	Output:
    17	- Markdown table for paper §3 / Appendix
    18	- Identifies which cells have insufficient N for paper-grade claims
    19	"""
    20	
    21	from __future__ import annotations
    22	
    23	import argparse
    24	import json
    25	import math
    26	from pathlib import Path
    27	from typing import List, Tuple
    28	
